  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Fill a large pot about halfway with hot water (from the tap); cover and bring to a boil over high heat."
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce."
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut cauliflower into 1-inch florets and slice stems into smaller pieces."
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the water comes to a boil, uncover, then add cauliflower, edamame, and salt; stir for a few seconds. Cook until cauliflower and edamame are tender-crisp, about 3 minutes. Drain and set aside to cool slightly."
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, place mayo, Dijon, vinegar, sugar, and spices in a medium bowl; whisk to combine the dressing."
    },
    {
      "text": "Peel and mince shallot. Add to the bowl with the dressing."
    },
    {
      "text": "Trim and small dice celery. Add to the bowl."
    },
    {
      "text": "Shave dill leaves off the stems; discard stems and mince the leaves. Add dill, cauliflower, and edamame to the bowl; stir to combine the salad."
    },
    {
      "text": "To serve, divide salad between bowls and enjoy!"
    }
  ]
